The function starts by checking if the input array has only one element, in which case the only possible permutation is the list containing that element. If the input array has more than one element, it loops through each element in the array and recursively calls the function with a subset of the array that does not include the current element. The result of each recursive call is then added to a list that contains all possible permutations of the original array. Finally, the function returns the list of lists.

