private int findMinFibonacciNumbers(int[] fibonacciNumbers, int[] memo, int k, int index) {
    if (k == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (index == fibonacciNumbers.length) {
        return -1;
    }
    if (memo[k] != -1) {
        return memo[k];
    }
    int minFibonacciNumbers = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
    for (int i = index; i < fibonacciNumbers.length; i++) {
        int currentFibonacciNumber = fibonacciNumbers[i];
        if (k < currentFibonacciNumber) {
            break;
        }
        int minFibonacciNumbersFromCurrent = findMinFibonacciNumbers(fibonacciNumbers, memo, k - currentFibonacciNumber, i);
        if (minFibonacciNumbersFromCurrent != -1) {
            minFibonacciNumbers = Math.min(minFibonacciNumbers, minFibonacciNumbersFromCurrent + 1);
        }
    }
    memo[k] = minFibonacciNumbers != Integer.MAX_VALUE ? minFibonacciNumbers : -1;
    return memo[k];
}
```
This code implements a memoized version of the recursive solution to the problem. The `memo` array is used to store the minimum number of Fibonacci numbers needed to sum to `k` for each `k` up to `k + 1`. The `findMinFibonacciNumbers` method takes the `fibonacciNumbers` array, the `memo` array, the current `k`, and the current `index` in the `fibonacciNumbers` array as input. If `k` is 0, the method returns 0. If `index` is equal to the length of the `fibonacciNumbers` array, the method returns -1 to indicate that no combination of Fibonacci numbers can sum to `k`. If the value of `memo[k]` is not -1, the method returns the value of `memo[k]` as the minimum number of Fibonacci numbers needed to sum to `k`.

Otherwise, the method calculates the minimum number of Fibonacci numbers needed to sum to `k` by looping through the `fibonacciNumbers` array starting from the current `index` and adding up the values of the Fibonacci numbers less than or equal to `k`. If the sum of the current Fibonacci number and the minimum number of Fibonacci numbers needed to sum to `k - currentFibonacciNumber` is less than or equal to the current minimum, the method updates the minimum and stores the value in `memo[k]`. The method then continues to the next iteration of the loop until the minimum has been determined or until the end of the `fibonacciNumbers` array has been reached. Finally, the method returns the minimum number of Fibonacci numbers needed to sum to `k`.

